WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.207
Before we start. This is a learning demonstration, not investment advice. It values a real

00:00:06.207 --> 00:00:12.415
company, Asbury Automotive, for teaching only, from public filings, and nothing in it is a

00:00:12.415 --> 00:00:18.622
recommendation to buy or sell anything. The narration is my voice, synthesized with my consent.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:25.429
We are going to value a company the way it is done on

00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:30.239
a desk. The company is Asbury Automotive Group, ticker ABG, a publicly traded franchised

00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:35.048
car dealer. Three annual reports, the 10-Ks for 2023, 2024 and 2025, one half-year

00:00:35.048 --> 00:00:39.858
update, and a share price for orientation at the end. That is the whole

00:00:39.858 --> 00:00:44.667
kit. Here is what you will be able to do when we are done.

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:49.477
You will be able to take the history out of those filings, decide what

00:00:49.477 --> 00:00:54.286
it does and does not tell you, write down one set of assumptions with

00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:59.095
a label on each one saying where it came from, project five years of

00:00:59.095 --> 00:01:03.905
income statement, balance sheet and cash flow that tie to each other, prove they

00:01:03.905 --> 00:01:08.714
tie with checks that can fail, and turn the cash flows into a value

00:01:08.714 --> 00:01:13.524
per share. That is the base case. One assumption set, one answer. Everything that

00:01:13.524 --> 00:01:18.333
follows in the second video, the what-ifs, the charts, the presentation, hangs off this.

00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:23.143
One rule before we start. Every number you see today comes from a filing

00:01:23.143 --> 00:01:27.952
or from arithmetic on a filing that you can see on the screen. When

00:01:27.952 --> 00:01:32.761
I use a judgment, I will say the word judgment. And a disclaimer, because

00:01:32.761 --> 00:01:37.571
we are using a real company: this is a learning demonstration, not investment advice.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:45.390
Seven lines, three years. Four from the income statement: revenue, gross profit, selling

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:49.910
general and administrative expense, which everyone calls SG and A, and net income. Three

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:54.430
from the balance sheet: inventory, property and equipment, and shareholders' equity. All in millions

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:58.951
of dollars. Read across the revenue line. Fourteen point eight billion, seventeen point two,

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:03.471
eighteen point zero. Read the net income line. Six hundred and two million, four

00:02:03.471 --> 00:02:07.991
hundred and thirty, four hundred and ninety-two. Revenue up more than twenty percent over

00:02:07.991 --> 00:02:12.511
two years, profit down. Hold that thought. Nothing in this grid is an estimate.

00:02:12.511 --> 00:02:17.031
The three accession numbers under the title are the filings' serial numbers at the

00:02:17.031 --> 00:02:21.551
SEC. The numbers were pulled through a data provider and every one was checked

00:02:21.551 --> 00:02:26.072
back to the 10-K; in a minute you will see why that check matters.

00:02:26.072 --> 00:02:30.592
Notice what is not here. No forecasts, no growth rate, no target price. We

00:02:30.592 --> 00:02:35.112
start from what the company actually reported, and we earn every assumption from it.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:44.099
Start with the most abused number in any forecast: growth. Reported revenue grew sixteen

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:49.788
percent in 2024 and four point seven percent in 2025. If you put four

00:02:49.788 --> 00:02:55.477
point seven percent into a model and compound it, you have already made your first

00:02:55.477 --> 00:03:01.166
mistake. Look at the second line. In December 2023 Asbury bought the Koons dealership

00:03:01.166 --> 00:03:06.854
group. Koons contributed two point eight billion of revenue in 2024. That is nineteen percent

00:03:06.854 --> 00:03:12.543
of the prior year's revenue, more than the entire growth rate. In July 2025

00:03:12.543 --> 00:03:18.232
Asbury bought Herb Chambers, which contributed one point one six billion in 2025, six

00:03:18.232 --> 00:03:23.921
point seven percent of the prior year. Reported growth was bought. Now the line that

00:03:23.921 --> 00:03:29.610
matters, highlighted. The company discloses same-store revenue, the stores it owned in both years,

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:35.299
split into new vehicles, used vehicles, parts and service, and finance and insurance. Add the

00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:40.988
four up for 2024 and 2025 and the stores Asbury already owned grew one

00:03:40.988 --> 00:03:46.677
point two percent. Not four point seven. One point two. That is the organic business.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:53.192
Two ratios run a car dealer. Gross margin, gross profit over revenue: eighteen point

00:03:53.192 --> 00:03:58.904
six percent, seventeen point two, seventeen point one. It fell and then stabilised. The company's

00:03:58.904 --> 00:04:04.616
own discussion tells you why: new-vehicle margins were unusually high in the shortage years

00:04:04.616 --> 00:04:10.328
and have come back down; that is how the company itself puts it. So the

00:04:10.328 --> 00:04:16.041
fall is not a trend to extrapolate; it is a one-time return to normal.

00:04:16.041 --> 00:04:21.753
The second ratio is the one you will not find in a textbook, and the

00:04:21.753 --> 00:04:27.465
one dealers actually manage: SG and A as a share of gross profit. It

00:04:27.465 --> 00:04:33.177
answers the question, what does it cost this company to earn a dollar of gross

00:04:33.177 --> 00:04:38.889
profit? Fifty-eight point seven cents, then sixty-four point one, then sixty-four point seven. That

00:04:38.889 --> 00:04:44.601
is the whole story of the falling net income. Revenue up, gross margin normal, and

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:50.313
the cost of running the stores rose faster than the gross profit they produced.

00:04:50.313 --> 00:04:56.025
Part of that, how much we cannot measure from the filings, is buying and integrating

00:04:56.025 --> 00:05:01.737
two large groups in two years. How fast it comes back down is the

00:05:01.737 --> 00:05:07.450
single biggest judgment in this valuation, and we will say so when we make it.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:13.529
Now the balance-sheet habits. Inventory days, inventory over cost of sales times three sixty-five:

00:05:13.529 --> 00:05:18.809
fifty-four, fifty-one, fifty-two. Stable. A dealer carries about fifty-two days of vehicles. The next

00:05:18.809 --> 00:05:24.088
line is the one that makes a dealer different from every other company you

00:05:24.088 --> 00:05:29.367
will model. Dealers do not pay cash for the cars on the lot. They

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:34.646
borrow against them, from the manufacturers' finance arms and from banks. Those inventory loans

00:05:34.646 --> 00:05:39.926
are called floor plan, and they cover eighty-six percent of inventory in 2024 and

00:05:39.926 --> 00:05:45.205
ninety-five percent in 2025. Two billion dollars of vehicles, funded by lenders who hold

00:05:45.205 --> 00:05:50.484
the cars as collateral. When inventory rises, the loan rises with it. We will

00:05:50.484 --> 00:05:55.764
model it exactly that way, and later I will show you what happens if

00:05:55.764 --> 00:06:01.043
you forget. Depreciation over property and equipment, roughly two point seven to two point

00:06:01.043 --> 00:06:06.322
nine percent. Steady. Now look at the two capital-spending lines together, because this is

00:06:06.322 --> 00:06:11.601
a trap that catches professionals. The 10-K says capital spending was one forty-two, three

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:16.881
oh eight, two oh five million. The standardised field from a data provider says

00:06:16.881 --> 00:06:22.160
one forty-two, one forty-six, and nineteen. Nineteen million. For a company with three billion

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:27.439
dollars of property. The provider's tag picked up the wrong line in 2025. If

00:06:27.439 --> 00:06:32.719
you had trusted it, your free cash flow would be nearly two hundred million

00:06:32.719 --> 00:06:37.998
too high. Every number from a data provider gets checked against the filing before

00:06:37.998 --> 00:06:43.277
it goes anywhere near a model. That check is the cheapest insurance you will

00:06:43.277 --> 00:06:48.556
ever buy. Impairment charges: one seventeen, one fifty, one forty-one. These are write-downs of

00:06:48.556 --> 00:06:53.836
franchise rights, the right to sell a brand in a territory, which a dealer

00:06:53.836 --> 00:06:59.115
carries as an asset. Non-cash, and they happen every year. A charge that recurs

00:06:59.115 --> 00:07:04.394
is not one-off, so we will carry it, but we will remember it is

00:07:04.394 --> 00:07:09.674
not cash. Effective tax rate: twenty-four point eight, twenty-five point two, twenty-five point seven

00:07:09.674 --> 00:07:14.953
percent. That is the twenty-one percent federal rate plus about four points of state

00:07:14.953 --> 00:07:20.232
tax, drifting up slightly. That is the history read. Now we turn it into assumptions.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:28.039
Stop on this screen for a minute, because it answers a question you

00:07:28.039 --> 00:07:32.547
will be asked in your first week at work: why is this in Python

00:07:32.547 --> 00:07:37.056
and not in a spreadsheet? Look at what is on the screen. Seven assumptions.

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:41.564
Each one has a name you can read, growth, gross margin, tax rate, and

00:07:41.564 --> 00:07:46.073
next to each one, in the same line, the label and the reason: judgment,

00:07:46.073 --> 00:07:50.581
history, guidance, and why. In a spreadsheet that number lives in a cell called

00:07:50.581 --> 00:07:55.090
C7, and the reason lives in your memory, or nowhere. Four things follow from

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:59.598
that, and you will see all four today. First, when you change one number,

00:07:59.598 --> 00:08:04.107
everything downstream reruns, every statement, every check, the value, and if something breaks the

00:08:04.107 --> 00:08:08.615
model stops and tells you which year and by how much. A spreadsheet recalculates

00:08:08.615 --> 00:08:13.124
silently. Second, this model has a test suite: forty-three tests that run in two

00:08:13.124 --> 00:08:17.632
seconds and prove the arithmetic still ties. Nobody tests a spreadsheet. Third, every change

00:08:17.632 --> 00:08:22.141
to an assumption is a line in a history you can read: who moved

00:08:22.141 --> 00:08:26.650
the growth rate, when, and from what. Fourth, and this is the part that

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:31.158
changes what the job is: you do not write most of this code. You

00:08:31.158 --> 00:08:35.667
describe the change in a sentence, your AI partner edits the model, and your

00:08:35.667 --> 00:08:40.175
job becomes judging whether the assumption is right. The skill that pays is the

00:08:40.175 --> 00:08:44.684
judgment, not the formula. And there is a door that opens from here. These

00:08:44.684 --> 00:08:49.192
same lines, with the assumptions behind a few sliders, become a small application. A

00:08:49.192 --> 00:08:53.701
colleague moves gross margin, watches the value move, and asks a better question than

00:08:53.701 --> 00:08:58.209
they would from a PDF. A student who can hand a portfolio manager a

00:08:58.209 --> 00:09:02.718
working, personalised valuation tool is doing something a spreadsheet builder cannot, and in my

00:09:02.718 --> 00:09:07.226
experience it is a thing people pay for. You will still be asked for

00:09:07.226 --> 00:09:11.735
the spreadsheet, and you will export one. But the thinking will have happened here.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:18.247
Here is the discipline. Every assumption is a named number, set in one

00:09:18.247 --> 00:09:23.965
place, with a label: history, guidance, or judgment. History means the number is a

00:09:23.965 --> 00:09:29.682
ratio we just computed and we are carrying it. Guidance means management said it.

00:09:29.682 --> 00:09:35.400
Judgment means we chose it, and we owe you the reason. Organic growth, one

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:41.117
point eight percent a year. Judgment. The stores already owned grew one point two;

00:09:41.117 --> 00:09:46.835
the industry grows with the economy at low single digits; we sit a little

00:09:46.835 --> 00:09:52.552
above the same-store figure and well below the bought four point seven. Acquisitions are

00:09:52.552 --> 00:09:58.270
excluded; if Asbury buys another group, that is a separate decision with its own

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:03.987
price tag. Gross margin, seventeen point zero five percent, essentially the 2025 margin,

00:10:03.987 --> 00:10:09.705
held flat. I label that judgment, not history, because holding it flat rather than

00:10:09.705 --> 00:10:15.422
extrapolating the decline is a choice. The reason for the choice is the one

00:10:15.422 --> 00:10:21.140
we just read: the shortage premium is gone. SG and A over gross profit.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:26.857
Judgment, and the big one. Sixty-six and a half percent in 2026, up from

00:10:26.857 --> 00:10:32.575
sixty-four point seven, because Herb Chambers was bought halfway through 2025 and the first

00:10:32.575 --> 00:10:38.292
full year of integration costs money. Then sixty-five and a half, then sixty-four and

00:10:38.292 --> 00:10:44.009
a half for the last three years. A recovery back near the 2024 level,

00:10:44.009 --> 00:10:49.727
not back to the fifty-nine percent of 2023. If you believe the cost savings

00:10:49.727 --> 00:10:55.444
from combining the groups come faster, the second video shows you exactly what

00:10:55.444 --> 00:11:01.162
that is worth. Depreciation, two point six eight percent of the opening property balance.

00:11:01.162 --> 00:11:06.879
History. Impairment, one hundred and twenty million a year. Judgment: below the three-year average

00:11:06.879 --> 00:11:12.597
of one thirty-six, a recurring non-cash charge we neither zero out nor inflate. Capital

00:11:12.597 --> 00:11:18.314
spending, two hundred and fifty million a year. Guidance: management's figure for 2026. Carrying

00:11:18.314 --> 00:11:24.032
it for five years is our judgment. Note the caveat on screen: the first

00:11:24.032 --> 00:11:29.749
half of 2026 ran hotter, around three thirty-nine annualised. That challenges the assumption; it

00:11:29.749 --> 00:11:35.467
does not yet replace it. Tax, twenty-five and a half percent. Judgment: between the

00:11:35.467 --> 00:11:41.184
three-year average of twenty-five point two and the 2025 rate of twenty-five point seven.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:47.241
Balance sheet and financing. Inventory days, fifty-two point two, history. Floor plan at ninety-five

00:11:47.241 --> 00:11:52.502
percent of inventory, history. Other working capital moves at zero point eight percent of

00:11:52.502 --> 00:11:57.763
the change in revenue, judgment, and it is tiny. Minimum cash, twenty-five million: this

00:11:57.763 --> 00:12:03.024
company runs on almost no cash, forty million at the end of 2025, because the

00:12:03.024 --> 00:12:08.285
floor plan does the funding. If cash would fall below twenty-five, the model draws

00:12:08.285 --> 00:12:13.546
a revolving credit line, the revolver, capped at eight hundred and fifty million at

00:12:13.546 --> 00:12:18.807
six percent. That is a safety net; in the base case it is never touched.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:24.003
Debt repayment, one hundred and fifty million a year, judgment. Share buyback,

00:12:24.003 --> 00:12:28.396
one hundred and fifty million a year, judgment, against actuals of two sixty,

00:12:28.396 --> 00:12:32.790
one eighty-five and one hundred over the three years. Interest rates: four point

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:37.183
six seven percent on the floor plan and five point four four on

00:12:37.183 --> 00:12:41.576
the term debt, which is 2025 interest expense divided by the opening balances.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:47.502
Two valuation numbers. Cost of equity, ten percent: the return the owners of this

00:12:47.502 --> 00:12:52.625
stock require. It is a round number, a little above what an average stock

00:12:52.625 --> 00:12:57.747
in the market earns today, and I am using it deliberately as a starting

00:12:57.747 --> 00:13:02.869
point. In the second video we measure Asbury's beta, how much the stock moves when

00:13:02.869 --> 00:13:07.992
the market moves, and put the real number in. Terminal growth, two and a

00:13:07.992 --> 00:13:13.114
half percent: how fast the cash flows grow after 2030, forever. It must stay

00:13:13.114 --> 00:13:18.236
below the cost of equity, and I will show you why. And seventeen point nine

00:13:18.236 --> 00:13:23.359
five million shares: the latest filed count, from the June 2026 quarterly balance sheet,

00:13:23.359 --> 00:13:28.481
forty point one million issued less twenty-two point one five million held in treasury.

00:13:28.481 --> 00:13:33.603
A year-end count would be a year stale; the company has been buying back stock.

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:38.100
Nineteen assumptions. Six from history, one from guidance, twelve judgments, plus one

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:41.799
fact, the share count. You can see all of them on three

00:13:41.799 --> 00:13:45.499
short screens. That is the standard: nothing buried in a cell somewhere.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:53.293
Now we build 2026. The function on screen is the entire model: about

00:13:53.293 --> 00:13:57.786
forty lines, and every line is one statement line. Read it the way

00:13:57.786 --> 00:14:02.279
you would read a spreadsheet column. In a spreadsheet, this is three tabs

00:14:02.279 --> 00:14:06.772
and a few hundred cells, and the only way to know what a

00:14:06.772 --> 00:14:11.265
cell does is to click on it. Here you can read the whole

00:14:11.265 --> 00:14:15.758
business logic top to bottom in one minute, and so can the colleague

00:14:15.758 --> 00:14:20.251
who reviews your work, and so can the AI that helps you change

00:14:20.251 --> 00:14:24.744
it. I want you to see the order, because the order is the method.

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:31.047
The income statement. Revenue: last year's seventeen thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine times one

00:14:31.047 --> 00:14:36.554
point zero one eight, eighteen thousand three hundred and twenty-three. Gross profit at seventeen

00:14:36.554 --> 00:14:42.061
point zero five percent, three thousand one hundred and twenty-four. SG and A at

00:14:42.061 --> 00:14:47.568
sixty-six and a half percent of that, two thousand and seventy-eight. Depreciation, opening property

00:14:47.568 --> 00:14:53.075
times two point six eight percent, eighty-two. Impairment, one twenty. Operating income, eight forty-four,

00:14:53.075 --> 00:14:58.582
down from eight sixty-one, because we made costs go up first. Interest is where

00:14:58.582 --> 00:15:04.089
the floor plan shows up again. Floor plan interest is the opening floor plan

00:15:04.089 --> 00:15:09.596
balance, two thousand and twenty-seven, times four point six seven percent: ninety-five million. Term

00:15:09.596 --> 00:15:15.103
debt interest is the opening debt, three thousand five hundred and seventy-two, times five

00:15:15.103 --> 00:15:20.610
point four four: one ninety-four. Pretax income five fifty-five. The 2025 figure of six

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:26.117
sixty-two included an eighty-million gain on selling dealerships; we do not forecast gains. Tax

00:15:26.117 --> 00:15:31.624
at twenty-five and a half percent, and net income four hundred and fourteen million.

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:37.780
The balance sheet. Inventory is cost of sales times fifty-two point two days over

00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:43.140
three sixty-five: two thousand one hundred and seventy-five. Property is opening plus two-fifty of

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:48.500
spending less depreciation: three thousand two hundred and thirty-eight. Other assets fall by the

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:53.860
impairment, because a write-down shrinks the asset it writes down. Floor plan is inventory

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:59.220
times ninety-five percent, two thousand and sixty-four. Term debt is opening less one fifty,

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:04.580
three thousand four hundred and twenty-two. Other liabilities held flat. Equity is opening plus

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:09.940
net income less the buyback, four thousand one hundred and fifty-five. And cash, highlighted,

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:15.300
one hundred and one point eight. Where did it come from? From the cash

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:20.659
flow statement, which we build next. Assets eleven thousand seven hundred and sixty-nine. Liabilities

00:16:20.659 --> 00:16:26.019
and equity eleven thousand seven hundred and sixty-nine. Difference zero point zero. The 2025

00:16:26.019 --> 00:16:31.379
column shows minus zero point two, which is the company's own rounding in the

00:16:31.379 --> 00:16:36.739
filing, and we carry it so you can see we did not hide it.

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:42.386
The cash flow statement, built as the flow to the owners. Start with

00:16:42.386 --> 00:16:47.233
net income, four fourteen. Add back the two charges that were not cash: depreciation

00:16:47.233 --> 00:16:52.079
eighty-two, impairment one twenty. Take out capital spending, two fifty. Take out the

00:16:52.079 --> 00:16:56.925
cash tied up in more inventory, thirty-nine, and in other working capital, two point

00:16:56.925 --> 00:17:01.772
six. Add back the increase in the floor plan, thirty-seven, because the lender

00:17:01.772 --> 00:17:06.618
funded ninety-five percent of that new inventory. Take out the debt repayment, one fifty.

00:17:06.618 --> 00:17:11.464
What is left is free cash flow to equity, two hundred and eleven

00:17:11.464 --> 00:17:16.311
million. That is the cash the business generates for its owners after the business

00:17:16.311 --> 00:17:21.157
has been fed and the lenders have been paid. That is the number

00:17:21.157 --> 00:17:26.003
we value. The buyback below it is how the owners take the cash out;

00:17:26.003 --> 00:17:30.850
it is a distribution, not the cash flow itself, so it does not

00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:35.696
change the value. Cash rises by sixty-one: two eleven in, one fifty out. Forty

00:17:35.696 --> 00:17:40.542
point four plus sixty-one is one hundred and one point eight, the cash

00:17:40.542 --> 00:17:45.389
on the balance sheet. Three statements, one number, nothing forced to make it balance.

00:17:48.690 --> 00:17:53.845
Five checks, all reading OK with a gap of zero. Assets equal liabilities plus

00:17:53.845 --> 00:17:59.000
equity. Cash on the balance sheet equals cash from the cash flow statement. Property

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:04.154
rolls forward. Debt rolls forward. Cash stays above the floor. A check that cannot

00:18:04.154 --> 00:18:09.309
fail is decoration. So let me make two of them fail, on purpose. But

00:18:09.309 --> 00:18:14.464
first, the rule, because I am not going to assume you will remember to look.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:19.393
This function is six lines and it is the most important six lines

00:18:19.393 --> 00:18:23.526
in the model. For every projected year it asks two questions: do assets equal

00:18:23.526 --> 00:18:27.659
liabilities plus equity, and is cash at or above the floor? If either

00:18:27.659 --> 00:18:31.793
answer is no, it does not print a warning. It stops the model. In

00:18:31.793 --> 00:18:35.926
a moment you will see the valuation cell call it first, which means

00:18:35.926 --> 00:18:40.059
the discounted cash flow cannot run on a balance sheet that does not balance.

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:45.169
Here is the rule, and it applies to every model you build in

00:18:45.169 --> 00:18:49.477
this course. One: every projected year, assets minus liabilities minus equity equals zero, printed,

00:18:49.477 --> 00:18:53.786
not assumed. Two: cash on the balance sheet equals opening cash plus the cash

00:18:53.786 --> 00:18:58.094
flow statement's net change. Three: cash stays at or above the floor, or the

00:18:58.094 --> 00:19:02.403
revolver line shows the draw. Four: the check block sits under every projection you

00:19:02.403 --> 00:19:06.712
hand in, and your valuation cell refuses to run without it. A model that

00:19:06.712 --> 00:19:11.020
does not show its checks has not been reviewed, by you or by anyone

